{"schemaVersion":1,"notes":[{"id":"039fcd2e-ec60-40e3-b8a1-e8972a832fea","title":"Feature Engineering","content":"The process of selecting or transforming input variables so a learning algorithm can use useful patterns in the data.","tags":["machine learning","features","data","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:31.104929300Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:31.104929300Z"},{"id":"055af5df-b126-4966-927e-f56a85e6442d","title":"PyTorch Tutorials","content":"Official tutorials for tensors, automatic differentiation, neural network training, data loading, and model deployment. Source: pytorch.org/tutorials.","tags":["resource","pytorch","documentation","deep learning"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":70,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.215891Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.215891Z"},{"id":"0e5abb05-b349-4192-bff9-f80119d226b9","title":"Topological Sorting","content":"Topological sorting orders the vertices of a directed acyclic graph so every prerequisite appears before the item that depends on it.","tags":["graph theory","graphs","prerequisites","algorithms"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":64,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.682623800Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.682623800Z"},{"id":"22e3f889-89b2-4571-bfa6-9f46fc5c972b","title":"Gradient Boosting","content":"Gradient boosting builds an ensemble of weak prediction models in sequence, with each new model reducing the loss left by earlier models.","tags":["machine learning","optimization","loss function","ensembles"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":72,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.499326200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.499326200Z"},{"id":"245421a4-8fe1-4a09-9e15-159025e39dde","title":"Loss Function","content":"A measure of how far a model prediction is from the desired result. Training algorithms adjust model parameters to reduce this value.","tags":["machine learning","optimization","gradients","training"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:24.076065900Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:24.076065900Z"},{"id":"299fe9a0-4621-4e8c-8635-9db4f5d4a184","title":"Attention Is All You Need","content":"Research paper introducing the Transformer architecture, which uses self-attention to model sequence relationships without recurrence. Source: Vaswani et al., 2017, arXiv:1706.03762.","tags":["attention","resource","transformers","deep learning"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":82,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.040773900Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.040773900Z"},{"id":"33bc6f5b-3103-4412-90b2-b5ef7b135949","title":"Dijkstra's algorithm","content":"Dijkstra's algorithm is a greedy algorithm that finds the shortest path from a starting node to all other nodes in a weighted grap","tags":["dsa","algorithm","graph"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":70,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T16:09:33.585590700Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T16:09:33.585590700Z"},{"id":"3ff147a9-b8f6-4b0f-82d2-dff2e14b8c18","title":"Minimum Spanning Trees","content":"A minimum spanning tree connects every vertex in a weighted undirected graph using the lowest possible total edge weight without cycles.","tags":["graph theory","optimization","graphs","algorithms"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":65,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.635061300Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.635061300Z"},{"id":"41884cce-d6c0-4df4-9ac7-6883f65e6bd2","title":"Batch Normalization","content":"A neural-network technique that normalizes intermediate activations during training to help stabilize and speed up optimization.","tags":["neural networks","normalization","training","deep learning"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:36.132392Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:36.132392Z"},{"id":"423a41c3-a09c-424f-b1d9-c2c228501333","title":"Model Evaluation","content":"The process of measuring a trained model with suitable metrics and data that was not used to fit it.","tags":["precision","metrics","validation","recall"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:43.045453900Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:43.045453900Z"},{"id":"482c0e6a-6859-407f-9f43-115c86300463","title":"Overfitting","content":"When a model learns details and noise in its training data so closely that it performs poorly on new examples.","tags":["regularization","machine learning","generalization","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:27.781269400Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:27.781269400Z"},{"id":"4a2df898-51f8-41ee-b3bb-c85ea5c7289a","title":"Summary: Model Generalization","content":"A model generalizes when it performs well on data beyond its training examples. Separate training and validation data, monitor overfitting, use regularization, and improve data coverage to support reliable predictions.","tags":["machine learning","summary","generalization","overfitting"],"type":"SUMMARY","importance":64,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.658561600Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.658561600Z"},{"id":"4f3cef50-7447-4a74-83fd-b06f4608734a","title":"How many clusters should k-means use?","content":"How can domain goals, cluster stability, and validation measures help choose k when no single value is obviously correct?","tags":["clustering","question","k-means","model evaluation"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":55,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.526403400Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.526403400Z"},{"id":"53241385-adc6-41a5-87ba-c0501ff62085","title":"Data Augmentation","content":"Data augmentation creates label-preserving variations of training examples to increase dataset diversity and improve model generalization.","tags":["machine learning","generalization","training","data"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":60,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.543331100Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.543331100Z"},{"id":"542a8496-f1c2-4df3-9566-4aa9de485a1f","title":"Gradient Descent","content":"An optimization method that iteratively adjusts model parameters in the direction that reduces the loss function. The learning rate controls the size of each update.","tags":["machine learning","optimization","gradients","training"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:23:50.723888700Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:23:50.723888700Z"},{"id":"6157d257-1476-402b-b7ee-f456ec4d6310","title":"Summary: Graph Traversal","content":"BFS explores a graph layer by layer and finds shortest paths when edges have equal cost. DFS follows a branch deeply before backtracking and is useful for reachability and component exploration.","tags":["summary","graphs","depth-first search","breadth-first search"],"type":"SUMMARY","importance":60,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.702639700Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.702639700Z"},{"id":"62206d0e-5596-4976-9337-7476c2266577","title":"Cross-Validation","content":"A method for estimating how well a model generalizes by repeatedly training and evaluating it on different partitions of the available data.","tags":["evaluation","validation","training","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:29.390453Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:29.390453Z"},{"id":"6468625e-52cb-4a5a-a9c4-77b67ceb0773","title":"Reinforcement Learning","content":"A learning approach where an agent improves its behavior by taking actions and receiving rewards from an environment.","tags":["agents","learning","rewards","policy"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:41.355313200Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:41.355313200Z"},{"id":"73287996-76aa-46b8-b5ff-658090b527d9","title":"The Elements of Statistical Learning","content":"Reference textbook covering statistical learning, regression, classification, model assessment, and ensemble methods. A useful companion for understanding the theory behind machine learning techniques.","tags":["machine learning","resource","textbook","statistics"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":76,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.103662Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.103662Z"},{"id":"7653ce8d-91f7-4918-9089-be2f9180cbad","title":"Introduction to Algorithms (CLRS)","content":"Textbook reference for algorithm design and analysis, including graph algorithms, sorting, data structures, and asymptotic complexity.","tags":["data structures","resource","textbook","algorithms"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":75,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.300409300Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.300409300Z"},{"id":"795c011e-56c9-4085-9b8b-5790c73477c6","title":"Embedding Space","content":"A vector space where items such as words or documents are represented so that meaningful similarity can be measured geometrically.","tags":["vectors","neural networks","embeddings","semantic search"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:33.098986200Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:33.098986200Z"},{"id":"7a5a96ec-0688-43f2-b550-4ac383184d3e","title":"Can graph communities improve a learning path?","content":"Could clusters of related notes help recommend a coherent study sequence while still respecting prerequisite relationships?","tags":["learning","graph theory","question","communities"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":57,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.571017300Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.571017300Z"},{"id":"7ac02e66-54d0-458d-a6d5-e8d763806e42","title":"Transformer Attention","content":"A mechanism that lets each token weigh information from other tokens in a sequence. Self-attention uses query, key, and value vectors to build context-aware representations.","tags":["attention","neural networks","embeddings","transformers"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:24:08.413737300Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:24:08.413737300Z"},{"id":"7f722c6a-59b1-42e0-8cfd-9e154ec8d617","title":"Convolutional Neural Network","content":"A neural-network architecture that uses local filters to detect spatial patterns, especially in images.","tags":["image processing","neural networks","features","deep learning"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:37.815628200Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:37.815628200Z"},{"id":"879868ed-7ffa-44d1-a152-ecbcb988b074","title":"Bayesian Networks","content":"A Bayesian network is a directed acyclic graph whose nodes represent random variables and whose edges encode conditional dependencies for probabilistic inference.","tags":["machine learning","probability","graphs","inference"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":70,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.334232900Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.334232900Z"},{"id":"98145ca6-ae3a-4695-b707-8647a6528cad","title":"Principal Component Analysis","content":"Principal component analysis projects correlated features onto orthogonal directions that preserve as much data variance as possible.","tags":["dimensionality reduction","machine learning","linear algebra","features"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":68,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.454163700Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.454163700Z"},{"id":"aee9d7ea-f95e-491c-b13e-0e06d92042d9","title":"Recurrent Neural Network","content":"A neural-network architecture that carries information through a sequence, making it useful for ordered or time-based data.","tags":["neural networks","time series","deep learning","sequence"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:39.648006300Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:39.648006300Z"},{"id":"algorithm-analysis","title":"Algorithm Analysis","content":"Analyze time and space cost using asymptotic notation.","tags":["graph","complexity","search","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"SUMMARY","importance":86,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"b26445ae-67d7-4653-bed0-8f914bf6bde5","title":"Epoch","content":"One complete pass through the training examples. Monitoring performance across epochs helps identify underfitting and overfitting.","tags":["machine learning","neural networks","training","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:26.088804900Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:26.088804900Z"},{"id":"backpropagation","title":"Backpropagation","content":"Compute gradients through a network using the chain rule.","tags":["neural","learning","model","ml","optimization"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":89,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"breadth-first-search","title":"Breadth-First Search","content":"BFS explores a graph level by level and finds shortest paths in unweighted graphs.","tags":["search","graphs","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":92,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"c25784c3-9648-4a25-a125-5f8826e28040","title":"How can we detect overfitting before deployment?","content":"Which validation signals and evaluation practices reveal that a model has memorized training examples and may fail on unseen production data?","tags":["question","model evaluation","overfitting","validation"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":59,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.478342700Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.478342700Z"},{"id":"c92ac07d-3bf1-4c0f-808c-9283e661cbc0","title":"Tokenization","content":"Breaking text into tokens that a language model can process, such as words, subwords, or characters.","tags":["text","language models","tokens","transformers"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:34.643230200Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:26:34.643230200Z"},{"id":"cpu-scheduling","title":"CPU Scheduling","content":"Scheduling policies choose which ready task receives processor time.","tags":["memory","process","thread","systems","scheduling","os"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":79,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"d25b171d-ee08-43a9-b52e-65e4e8ce4739","title":"Regularization","content":"Techniques that discourage a model from fitting noise in its training data. L1 and L2 penalties add constraints to the learning objective and can improve generalization.","tags":["machine learning","generalization","overfitting","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":50,"createdAt":"2026-10-19T03:24:02.408022700Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-19T03:24:02.408022700Z"},{"id":"d265e5e8-1ef1-4b89-af52-93c5ce54db8c","title":"What makes a useful similarity threshold?","content":"How should a knowledge system balance missed relationships against noisy links when turning note similarity scores into automatic suggestions?","tags":["knowledge graphs","question","jaccard","similarity"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":56,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.616787700Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.616787700Z"},{"id":"d8f53900-5731-4564-9c37-e50d5b1a8b02","title":"scikit-learn User Guide","content":"Official guide to supervised and unsupervised estimators, preprocessing, model selection, evaluation, and pipelines. Source: scikit-learn.org/stable/user_guide.html.","tags":["machine learning","resource","scikit-learn","documentation"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":69,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.261328200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.261328200Z"},{"id":"dbd02b5b-5707-47f7-8b6b-35eb4114c37d","title":"K-Means Clustering","content":"K-means partitions observations into k clusters by repeatedly assigning each point to its nearest centroid and updating the centroids.","tags":["clustering","machine learning","optimization","unsupervised learning"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":66,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.418190200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:01:25.418190200Z"},{"id":"depth-first-search","title":"Depth-First Search","content":"DFS explores one branch deeply before backtracking.","tags":["search","graphs","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":83,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"dsa-structures","title":"Data Structures","content":"Ways to organize data for efficient operations.","tags":["search","graph","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":90,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"ee5b8393-17ce-4ca6-b522-edf766a3adc7","title":"Dive into Deep Learning","content":"Interactive open textbook with executable explanations and code for neural networks, computer vision, sequence models, and attention. Source: d2l.ai.","tags":["tutorial","neural networks","resource","deep learning"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":68,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.336559100Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.336559100Z"},{"id":"efe200a1-c0f2-4460-ad40-b7eceb241eb9","title":"A* Search","content":"A* search combines the path cost so far with a heuristic estimate to guide graph exploration toward a goal efficiently.","tags":["search","graphs","algorithms","pathfinding"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":66,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.586012Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.586012Z"},{"id":"embeddings","title":"Embeddings","content":"Dense vectors represent items so useful similarities can be computed.","tags":["neural","model","similarity","ml","learning"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":78,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"f0b03071-d0ab-4681-88e4-be42c766fc01","title":"Deep Learning by Goodfellow, Bengio, and Courville","content":"Textbook introducing neural networks, optimization, convolutional networks, sequence models, and practical deep learning research.","tags":["neural networks","resource","textbook","deep learning"],"type":"RESOURCE","importance":77,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.152730100Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.152730100Z"},{"id":"f93c174b-2075-4035-9492-9155880876ad","title":"How should we choose a distance metric for embeddings?","content":"Which properties of an embedding task determine whether cosine similarity, Euclidean distance, or another metric gives the most useful nearest neighbors?","tags":["machine learning","question","embeddings","similarity"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":58,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.381784600Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.381784600Z"},{"id":"fc63d418-6fec-41b8-a02d-a5ba271f51e5","title":"When should BFS be replaced by Dijkstra's algorithm?","content":"How does the presence of non-uniform edge weights change the correctness of breadth-first search, and when is a priority-queue shortest-path method necessary?","tags":["dijkstra","question","graphs","breadth-first search"],"type":"QUESTION","importance":61,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.414594200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T17:04:43.414594200Z"},{"id":"fdf69dce-86cc-474e-af47-544253770a84","title":"Dynamic Programming","content":"Dynamic programming solves overlapping subproblems once and reuses their results to build an optimal solution for a larger problem.","tags":["optimization","algorithms","problem solving","recursion"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":73,"createdAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.723346200Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-14T16:57:27.723346200Z"},{"id":"graph-theory","title":"Graph Theory","content":"Graphs model vertices connected by edges and support traversal and path problems.","tags":["search","graphs","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":95,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"jaccard-index","title":"Jaccard Similarity","content":"Set similarity is intersection size divided by union size.","tags":["graph","similarity","search","algorithms","dsa"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":76,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"machine-learning","title":"Machine Learning","content":"Models learn useful patterns from examples and data.","tags":["ml","neural","learning","model"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":94,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z"},{"id":"memory-management","title":"Memory Management","content":"Virtual memory maps process addresses to physical memory and storage.","tags":["memory","process","thread","systems","scheduling","os"],"type":"CONCEPT","importance":85,"createdAt":"2026-01-15T12:00:00Z","upd